### Description

Cancel an approval task. Once canceled the task enters the final status `CANCELED` and can no longer be released; a new approval must be initiated if the operation is still needed.

Only a task waiting for approval (`PENDING`) can be canceled. Calling this API on a task that has already been released, rejected, canceled or failed returns a "status not allowed" error. Canceling only affects the approval task on the Job side and **does not notify the approval channel**: the ticket in the channel must be handled by the approver.

When a cancellation races with a release, **whichever grabs the pending status first wins**. If the release gets there first, this API returns a "status not allowed" error carrying the current status of the task (such as `EXECUTING`), which means **the cancellation did not take effect and the operation is already running**; the other way round, the release returns the same kind of error. So never treat that error as "canceled".

Only approval tasks created by the same user through the same application can be canceled. In every other case the "approval task does not exist" error is returned.

{% include '_generic_v4_approval_flow.md.j2' %}

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| approval_task_id | string | Yes | Approval task ID returned by the initiating API. Only a task waiting for approval can be canceled |

### Request Parameters Example

- POST

```json
{
    "approval_task_id": "5f9c1d1a3f2b4a1e9f2d7c1b2e3a4d5f"
}
```

