### Response Parameters

{% include '_generic_v4_response.md.j2' %}

#### data

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| approval_task_id | string | Approval task ID |
| status | string | Approval task status. Always `CANCELED` (canceled) after a successful cancellation |
| operation_type | string | Operation type. Options: `FAST_EXECUTE_SCRIPT` (fast execute script), `FAST_TRANSFER_FILE` (fast transfer file), `EXECUTE_JOB_PLAN` (launch a job plan), `CREATE_JOB_PLAN` (create a job plan), `SAVE_CRON` (save a cron job), `UPDATE_CRON_STATUS` (enable or disable a cron job) |
| approval_channel | string | Approval channel. Options: `IMATE` (IMate approval channel) |
| approval_ticket_id | string | Bound approval ticket ID, `null` when not bound yet. Canceling does not notify the approval channel; the ticket in the channel must be handled by the approver |
| creator | string | Creator of the approval task |
| create_time | long | Moment the task was initiated, Unix timestamp in milliseconds |
| expire_at | long | Expiry moment, Unix timestamp in milliseconds |
| approver | string | Approver. A cancelable task has no approval decision yet, so this field is `null` |
| approved_at | long | Approval moment, Unix timestamp in milliseconds. A cancelable task has no approval decision yet, so this field is `null` |
| execute_result | object | Operation result. A canceled task was never executed, so this field is always `null` |
| result_unknown | boolean | Unknown-result flag. Always `false` for a cancellation |
| message | string | Human-readable message |
